   "subject": "Spatial hierarchy",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">HI all,<div><br></div><div>I&#39;m building a model with a spatial hierarchy: all LSOAs fit inside a unique LAD. The model is as follows</div><div><br></div><div><div style=\"color:rgb(212,212,212);background-color:rgb(30,30,30);font-family:Menlo,Monaco,&quot;Courier New&quot;,monospace;font-size:12px;line-height:18px;white-space:pre\"><div><span style=\"color:#9cdcfe\">code</span> &lt;- <span style=\"color:#9cdcfe\">nimbleCode</span>({</div><div>    <span style=\"color:#6a9955\"># PRIORS</span></div><br><div>    <span style=\"color:#6a9955\"># COMMON TERMS</span></div><div>    <span style=\"color:#9cdcfe\">alpha0</span> <span style=\"color:#569cd6\">~</span> <span style=\"color:#dcdcaa\">dnorm</span>(<span style=\"color:#b5cea8\">0</span>, <span style=\"color:#b5cea8\">0.00001</span>)</div><div>    <span style=\"color:#9cdcfe\">beta0</span>  <span style=\"color:#569cd6\">~</span> <span style=\"color:#dcdcaa\">dnorm</span>(<span style=\"color:#b5cea8\">0</span>, <span style=\"color:#b5cea8\">0.00001</span>)</div><div>    </div><div>    <span style=\"color:#6a9955\"># AREA TERMS -- random effects for intercepts and slopes</span></div><div>    </div><div>    <span style=\"color:#6a9955\"># LAD terms</span></div><div>    <span style=\"color:#c586c0\">for</span>(<span style=\"color:#9cdcfe\">j_LAD</span> <span style=\"color:#c586c0\">in</span> <span style=\"color:#b5cea8\">1</span><span style=\"color:#569cd6\">:</span><span style=\"color:#9cdcfe\">N_LAD</span>){</div><div>        <span style=\"color:#9cdcfe\">alpha_LAD</span>[<span style=\"color:#9cdcfe\">j_LAD</span>] <span style=\"color:#569cd6\">~</span> <span style=\"color:#dcdcaa\">dnorm</span>(<span style=\"color:#9cdcfe\">alpha0</span>, <span style=\"color:#9cdcfe\">tau_alpha_LAD</span>) <span style=\"color:#6a9955\"># centred on common terms</span></div><div>        <span style=\"color:#9cdcfe\">beta_LAD</span>[<span style=\"color:#9cdcfe\">j_LAD</span>] <span style=\"color:#569cd6\">~</span> <span style=\"color:#dcdcaa\">dnorm</span>(<span style=\"color:#9cdcfe\">beta0</span>, <span style=\"color:#9cdcfe\">tau_beta_LAD</span>)</div><div>    }</div><div>    <span style=\"color:#9cdcfe\">sigma_alpha_LAD</span> <span style=\"color:#569cd6\">~</span> <span style=\"color:#dcdcaa\">dunif</span>(<span style=\"color:#b5cea8\">0</span>,<span style=\"color:#b5cea8\">2</span>)</div><div>    <span style=\"color:#9cdcfe\">tau_alpha_LAD</span> &lt;- <span style=\"color:#9cdcfe\">pow</span>(<span style=\"color:#9cdcfe\">sigma_alpha_LAD</span>,-<span style=\"color:#b5cea8\">2</span>)</div><div>    <span style=\"color:#9cdcfe\">sigma_beta_LAD</span>  <span style=\"color:#569cd6\">~</span> <span style=\"color:#dcdcaa\">dunif</span>(<span style=\"color:#b5cea8\">0</span>,<span style=\"color:#b5cea8\">2</span>)</div><div>    <span style=\"color:#9cdcfe\">tau_beta_LAD</span>  &lt;- <span style=\"color:#9cdcfe\">pow</span>(<span style=\"color:#9cdcfe\">sigma_beta_LAD</span>,-<span style=\"color:#b5cea8\">2</span>)</div><br><div>    <span style=\"color:#6a9955\"># LSOA terms</span></div><div>    <span style=\"color:#c586c0\">for</span>(<span style=\"color:#9cdcfe\">j</span> <span style=\"color:#c586c0\">in</span> <span style=\"color:#b5cea8\">1</span><span style=\"color:#569cd6\">:</span><span style=\"color:#9cdcfe\">N_LSOA</span>){</div><div>        <span style=\"color:#9cdcfe\">id_LAD</span> &lt;- <span style=\"color:#dcdcaa\">filter</span>(<span style=\"color:#9cdcfe\">mortality_m</span>, <span style=\"color:#9cdcfe\">LSOA.id</span> == <span style=\"color:#9cdcfe\">j</span>)<span style=\"color:#569cd6\">$</span><span style=\"color:#9cdcfe\">LAD.id</span>[<span style=\"color:#b5cea8\">1</span>] <span style=\"color:#6a9955\"># picks out LAD for jth LSOA</span></div><div>        <span style=\"color:#9cdcfe\">alpha1</span>[<span style=\"color:#9cdcfe\">j</span>] <span style=\"color:#569cd6\">~</span> <span style=\"color:#dcdcaa\">dnorm</span>(<span style=\"color:#9cdcfe\">alpha_LAD</span>[<span style=\"color:#9cdcfe\">id_LAD</span>], <span style=\"color:#9cdcfe\">tau_alpha1</span>) <span style=\"color:#6a9955\"># centred on LAD terms</span></div><div>        <span style=\"color:#9cdcfe\">beta1</span>[<span style=\"color:#9cdcfe\">j</span>]  <span style=\"color:#569cd6\">~</span> <span style=\"color:#dcdcaa\">dnorm</span>(<span style=\"color:#9cdcfe\">beta_LAD</span>[<span style=\"color:#9cdcfe\">id_LAD</span>], <span style=\"color:#9cdcfe\">tau_beta1</span>)</div><div>    }</div><div>    <span style=\"color:#9cdcfe\">sigma_alpha1</span> <span style=\"color:#569cd6\">~</span> <span style=\"color:#dcdcaa\">dunif</span>(<span style=\"color:#b5cea8\">0</span>,<span style=\"color:#b5cea8\">2</span>)</div><div>    <span style=\"color:#9cdcfe\">tau_alpha1</span> &lt;- <span style=\"color:#9cdcfe\">pow</span>(<span style=\"color:#9cdcfe\">sigma_alpha1</span>,-<span style=\"color:#b5cea8\">2</span>)</div><div>    <span style=\"color:#9cdcfe\">sigma_beta1</span>  <span style=\"color:#569cd6\">~</span> <span style=\"color:#dcdcaa\">dunif</span>(<span style=\"color:#b5cea8\">0</span>,<span style=\"color:#b5cea8\">2</span>)</div><div>    <span style=\"color:#9cdcfe\">tau_beta1</span>  &lt;- <span style=\"color:#9cdcfe\">pow</span>(<span style=\"color:#9cdcfe\">sigma_beta1</span>,-<span style=\"color:#b5cea8\">2</span>)</div><br><div>    <span style=\"color:#6a9955\"># Put all parameters together into indexed lograte</span></div><div>    <span style=\"color:#c586c0\">for</span>(<span style=\"color:#9cdcfe\">a</span> <span style=\"color:#c586c0\">in</span> <span style=\"color:#b5cea8\">1</span><span style=\"color:#569cd6\">:</span><span style=\"color:#9cdcfe\">N_age_groups</span>){</div><div>        <span style=\"color:#c586c0\">for</span>(<span style=\"color:#9cdcfe\">j</span> <span style=\"color:#c586c0\">in</span> <span style=\"color:#b5cea8\">1</span><span style=\"color:#569cd6\">:</span><span style=\"color:#9cdcfe\">N_LSOA</span>){</div><div>            <span style=\"color:#c586c0\">for</span>(<span style=\"color:#9cdcfe\">t</span> <span style=\"color:#c586c0\">in</span> <span style=\"color:#b5cea8\">1</span><span style=\"color:#569cd6\">:</span><span style=\"color:#9cdcfe\">N_year</span>){</div><div>                <span style=\"color:#9cdcfe\">lograte</span>[<span style=\"color:#9cdcfe\">a</span>, <span style=\"color:#9cdcfe\">j</span>, <span style=\"color:#9cdcfe\">t</span>] &lt;- <span style=\"color:#9cdcfe\">alpha1</span>[<span style=\"color:#9cdcfe\">j</span>] + <span style=\"color:#9cdcfe\">beta1</span>[<span style=\"color:#9cdcfe\">j</span>] * (<span style=\"color:#9cdcfe\">t</span> - <span style=\"color:#b5cea8\">8</span>)</div><div>            }</div><div>        }</div><div>    }</div><br><div>    <span style=\"color:#6a9955\"># LIKELIHOOD</span></div><div>    <span style=\"color:#6a9955\"># N total number of cells, i.e. ages*years*areas(*sex)</span></div><div>    <span style=\"color:#c586c0\">for</span> (<span style=\"color:#9cdcfe\">i</span> <span style=\"color:#c586c0\">in</span> <span style=\"color:#b5cea8\">1</span><span style=\"color:#569cd6\">:</span><span style=\"color:#9cdcfe\">N</span>) {</div><div>        <span style=\"color:#6a9955\"># y is number of deaths in that cell, assumed Poisson </span></div><div>        <span style=\"color:#6a9955\"># mu is predicted number of deaths in that cell</span></div><div>        <span style=\"color:#9cdcfe\">y</span>[<span style=\"color:#9cdcfe\">i</span>] <span style=\"color:#569cd6\">~</span> <span style=\"color:#dcdcaa\">dpois</span>(<span style=\"color:#9cdcfe\">mu</span>[<span style=\"color:#9cdcfe\">i</span>])</div><div>        <span style=\"color:#dcdcaa\">log</span>(<span style=\"color:#9cdcfe\">mu</span>[<span style=\"color:#9cdcfe\">i</span>]) &lt;- <span style=\"color:#dcdcaa\">log</span>(<span style=\"color:#9cdcfe\">n</span>[<span style=\"color:#9cdcfe\">i</span>]) + <span style=\"color:#9cdcfe\">lograte</span>[<span style=\"color:#9cdcfe\">age</span>[<span style=\"color:#9cdcfe\">i</span>], <span style=\"color:#9cdcfe\">LSOA</span>[<span style=\"color:#9cdcfe\">i</span>], <span style=\"color:#9cdcfe\">yr</span>[<span style=\"color:#9cdcfe\">i</span>]]</div><div>    }</div><div>})</div></div></div><div><br></div><div>Currently I&#39;m using dplyr&#39;s filter method to pick out the right LAD corresponding to the LSOA in that loop (nimble did not like [, ] slicing), but I get the following error:</div><div><br></div><div><pre style=\"font-family:Monaco,monospace,monospace;font-size:12px;outline:none;border-width:initial;border-style:none;word-break:break-all;line-height:1.45;white-space:pre-wrap!important\"><span><font color=\"#000000\">Error in getSymbolicParentNodesRecurse(x, constNames, indexNames, nimbleFunctionNames,  : \r\n  R function &#39;filter&#39; has arguments that cannot be evaluated; either the function must be a nimbleFunction or values for the following inputs must be specified as constants in the model: mortality_m,LSOA.id.</font></span></pre></div><div><br></div><div>Is there a quick workaround for what seems a fairly straightforward problem of calling the LAD that the LSOA lies within?</div><div><br></div><div>Best,</div><div><br></div><div>Theo</div></div>"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "9GZLnBhtBAAJ",
   "from": "Heather Gaya",
   "author": "f97d21be02e5ed9b",
   "date": "2020-03-11T18:46:50Z",
   "subject": "Re: Spatial hierarchy",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">One possible solution, if I understand your question correctly, would be to use a &quot;grid lookup&quot; type approach. <div><br></div><div>Give nimble a data object with id_LADs and have it pull from that.  For instance, the object grid.lookup could be a N_LAD X N_LSOA matrix with each entry representing the id for that LAD/LSOA combo. You could then call:</div><div> </div>alpha1[J_LAD,j] ~ dnorm(alpha_LAD[grid.lookup[j_LAD,j]], tau_alpha1) or similar. </div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div><br></div><div><br><div><br></div><div><div><br></div><div><br>On Wednesday, March 11, 2020 at 2:29:19 PM UTC-4, Theo Rashid wrote:<blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0;margin-left:0.8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\">HI all,<div><br></div><div>I&#39;m building a model with a spatial hierarchy: all LSOAs fit inside a unique LAD. The model is as follows</div><div><br></div><div><div style=\"color:rgb(212,212,212);background-color:rgb(30,30,30);font-family:Menlo,Monaco,&quot;Courier New&quot;,monospace;font-size:12px;line-height:18px;white-space:pre\"><div><span style=\"color:#9cdcfe\">code</span> &lt;- <span style=\"color:#9cdcfe\">nimbleCode</span>({</div><div>    <span style=\"color:#6a9955\"># PRIORS</span></div><br><div>    <span style=\"color:#6a9955\"># COMMON TERMS</span></div><div>    <span style=\"color:#9cdcfe\">alpha0</span> <span style=\"color:#569cd6\">~</span> <span style=\"color:#dcdcaa\">dnorm</span>(<span style=\"color:#b5cea8\">0</span>, <span style=\"color:#b5cea8\">0.00001</span>)</div><div>    <span style=\"color:#9cdcfe\">beta0</span>  <span style=\"color:#569cd6\">~</span> <span style=\"color:#dcdcaa\">dnorm</span>(<span style=\"color:#b5cea8\">0</span>, <span style=\"color:#b5cea8\">0.00001</span>)</div><div>    </div><div>    <span style=\"color:#6a9955\"># AREA TERMS -- random effects for intercepts and slopes</span></div><div>    </div><div>    <span style=\"color:#6a9955\"># LAD terms</span></div><div>    <span style=\"color:#c586c0\">for</span>(<span style=\"color:#9cdcfe\">j_LAD</span> <span style=\"color:#c586c0\">in</span> <span style=\"color:#b5cea8\">1</span><span style=\"color:#569cd6\">:</span><span style=\"color:#9cdcfe\">N_LAD</span>){</div><div>        <span style=\"color:#9cdcfe\">alpha_LAD</span>[<span style=\"color:#9cdcfe\">j_LAD</span>] <span style=\"color:#569cd6\">~</span> <span style=\"color:#dcdcaa\">dnorm</span>(<span style=\"color:#9cdcfe\">alpha0</span>, <span style=\"color:#9cdcfe\">tau_alpha_LAD</span>) <span style=\"color:#6a9955\"># centred on common terms</span></div><div>        <span style=\"color:#9cdcfe\">beta_LAD</span>[<span style=\"color:#9cdcfe\">j_LAD</span>] <span style=\"color:#569cd6\">~</span> <span style=\"color:#dcdcaa\">dnorm</span>(<span style=\"color:#9cdcfe\">beta0</span>, <span style=\"color:#9cdcfe\">tau_beta_LAD</span>)</div><div>    }</div><div>    <span style=\"color:#9cdcfe\">sigma_alpha_LAD</span> <span style=\"color:#569cd6\">~</span> <span style=\"color:#dcdcaa\">dunif</span>(<span style=\"color:#b5cea8\">0</span>,<span style=\"color:#b5cea8\">2</span>)</div><div>    <span style=\"color:#9cdcfe\">tau_alpha_LAD</span> &lt;- <span style=\"color:#9cdcfe\">pow</span>(<span style=\"color:#9cdcfe\">sigma_alpha_LAD</span>,-<span style=\"color:#b5cea8\">2</span>)</div><div>    <span style=\"color:#9cdcfe\">sigma_beta_LAD</span>  <span style=\"color:#569cd6\">~</span> <span style=\"color:#dcdcaa\">dunif</span>(<span style=\"color:#b5cea8\">0</span>,<span style=\"color:#b5cea8\">2</span>)</div><div>    <span style=\"color:#9cdcfe\">tau_beta_LAD</span>  &lt;- <span style=\"color:#9cdcfe\">pow</span>(<span style=\"color:#9cdcfe\">sigma_beta_LAD</span>,-<span style=\"color:#b5cea8\">2</span>)</div><br><div>    <span style=\"color:#6a9955\"># LSOA terms</span></div><div>    <span style=\"color:#c586c0\">for</span>(<span style=\"color:#9cdcfe\">j</span> <span style=\"color:#c586c0\">in</span> <span style=\"color:#b5cea8\">1</span><span style=\"color:#569cd6\">:</span><span style=\"color:#9cdcfe\">N_LSOA</span>){</div><div>        <span style=\"color:#9cdcfe\">id_LAD</span> &lt;- <span style=\"color:#dcdcaa\">filter</span>(<span style=\"color:#9cdcfe\">mortality_m</span>, <span style=\"color:#9cdcfe\">LSOA.id</span> == <span style=\"color:#9cdcfe\">j</span>)<span style=\"color:#569cd6\">$</span><span style=\"color:#9cdcfe\">LAD.id</span>[<span style=\"color:#b5cea8\">1</span>] <span style=\"color:#6a9955\"># picks out LAD for jth LSOA</span></div><div>        <span style=\"color:#9cdcfe\">alpha1</span>[<span style=\"color:#9cdcfe\">j</span>] <span style=\"color:#569cd6\">~</span> <span style=\"color:#dcdcaa\">dnorm</span>(<span style=\"color:#9cdcfe\">alpha_LAD</span>[<span style=\"color:#9cdcfe\">id_LAD</span>], <span style=\"color:#9cdcfe\">tau_alpha1</span>) <span style=\"color:#6a9955\"># centred on LAD terms</span></div><div>        <span style=\"color:#9cdcfe\">beta1</span>[<span style=\"color:#9cdcfe\">j</span>]  <span style=\"color:#569cd6\">~</span> <span style=\"color:#dcdcaa\">dnorm</span>(<span style=\"color:#9cdcfe\">beta_LAD</span>[<span style=\"color:#9cdcfe\">id_LAD</span>], <span style=\"color:#9cdcfe\">tau_beta1</span>)</div><div>    }</div><div>    <span style=\"color:#9cdcfe\">sigma_alpha1</span> <span style=\"color:#569cd6\">~</span> <span style=\"color:#dcdcaa\">dunif</span>(<span style=\"color:#b5cea8\">0</span>,<span style=\"color:#b5cea8\">2</span>)</div><div>    <span style=\"color:#9cdcfe\">tau_alpha1</span> &lt;- <span style=\"color:#9cdcfe\">pow</span>(<span style=\"color:#9cdcfe\">sigma_alpha1</span>,-<span style=\"color:#b5cea8\">2</span>)</div><div>    <span style=\"color:#9cdcfe\">sigma_beta1</span>  <span style=\"color:#569cd6\">~</span> <span style=\"color:#dcdcaa\">dunif</span>(<span style=\"color:#b5cea8\">0</span>,<span style=\"color:#b5cea8\">2</span>)</div><div>    <span style=\"color:#9cdcfe\">tau_beta1</span>  &lt;- <span style=\"color:#9cdcfe\">pow</span>(<span style=\"color:#9cdcfe\">sigma_beta1</span>,-<span style=\"color:#b5cea8\">2</span>)</div><br><div>    <span style=\"color:#6a9955\"># Put all parameters together into indexed lograte</span></div><div>    <span style=\"color:#c586c0\">for</span>(<span style=\"color:#9cdcfe\">a</span> <span style=\"color:#c586c0\">in</span> <span style=\"color:#b5cea8\">1</span><span style=\"color:#569cd6\">:</span><span style=\"color:#9cdcfe\">N_age_groups</span>){</div><div>        <span style=\"color:#c586c0\">for</span>(<span style=\"color:#9cdcfe\">j</span> <span style=\"color:#c586c0\">in</span> <span style=\"color:#b5cea8\">1</span><span style=\"color:#569cd6\">:</span><span style=\"color:#9cdcfe\">N_LSOA</span>){</div><div>            <span style=\"color:#c586c0\">for</span>(<span style=\"color:#9cdcfe\">t</span> <span style=\"color:#c586c0\">in</span> <span style=\"color:#b5cea8\">1</span><span style=\"color:#569cd6\">:</span><span style=\"color:#9cdcfe\">N_year</span>){</div><div>                <span style=\"color:#9cdcfe\">lograte</span>[<span style=\"color:#9cdcfe\">a</span>, <span style=\"color:#9cdcfe\">j</span>, <span style=\"color:#9cdcfe\">t</span>] &lt;- <span style=\"color:#9cdcfe\">alpha1</span>[<span style=\"color:#9cdcfe\">j</span>] + <span style=\"color:#9cdcfe\">beta1</span>[<span style=\"color:#9cdcfe\">j</span>] * (<span style=\"color:#9cdcfe\">t</span> - <span style=\"color:#b5cea8\">8</span>)</div><div>            }</div><div>        }</div><div>    }</div><br><div>    <span style=\"color:#6a9955\"># LIKELIHOOD</span></div><div>    <span style=\"color:#6a9955\"># N total number of cells, i.e. ages*years*areas(*sex)</span></div><div>    <span style=\"color:#c586c0\">for</span> (<span style=\"color:#9cdcfe\">i</span> <span style=\"color:#c586c0\">in</span> <span style=\"color:#b5cea8\">1</span><span style=\"color:#569cd6\">:</span><span style=\"color:#9cdcfe\">N</span>) {</div><div>        <span style=\"color:#6a9955\"># y is number of deaths in that cell, assumed Poisson </span></div><div>        <span style=\"color:#6a9955\"># mu is predicted number of deaths in that cell</span></div><div>        <span style=\"color:#9cdcfe\">y</span>[<span style=\"color:#9cdcfe\">i</span>] <span style=\"color:#569cd6\">~</span> <span style=\"color:#dcdcaa\">dpois</span>(<span style=\"color:#9cdcfe\">mu</span>[<span style=\"color:#9cdcfe\">i</span>])</div><div>        <span style=\"color:#dcdcaa\">log</span>(<span style=\"color:#9cdcfe\">mu</span>[<span style=\"color:#9cdcfe\">i</span>]) &lt;- <span style=\"color:#dcdcaa\">log</span>(<span style=\"color:#9cdcfe\">n</span>[<span style=\"color:#9cdcfe\">i</span>]) + <span style=\"color:#9cdcfe\">lograte</span>[<span style=\"color:#9cdcfe\">age</span>[<span style=\"color:#9cdcfe\">i</span>], <span style=\"color:#9cdcfe\">LSOA</span>[<span style=\"color:#9cdcfe\">i</span>], <span style=\"color:#9cdcfe\">yr</span>[<span style=\"color:#9cdcfe\">i</span>]]</div><div>    }</div><div>})</div></div></div><div><br></div><div>Currently I&#39;m using dplyr&#39;s filter method to pick out the right LAD corresponding to the LSOA in that loop (nimble did not like [, ] slicing), but I get the following error:</div><div><br></div><div><pre style=\"font-family:Monaco,monospace,monospace;font-size:12px;outline:none;border-width:initial;border-style:none;word-break:break-all;line-height:1.45;white-space:pre-wrap!important\"><span><font color=\"#000000\">Error in getSymbolicParentNodesRecurse(x, constNames, indexNames, nimbleFunctionNames,  : \r\n  R function &#39;filter&#39; has arguments that cannot be evaluated; either the function must be a nimbleFunction or values for the following inputs must be specified as constants in the model: mortality_m,LSOA.id.</font></span></pre></div><div><br></div><div>Is there a quick workaround for what seems a fairly straightforward problem of calling the LAD that the LSOA lies within?</div><div><br></div><div>Best,</div><div><br></div><div>Theo</div></div></blockquote></div></div></div></div>"
    ]
   ]
