  {
   "id": "rJowCz_aAwAJ",
   "from": "Perry de Valpine",
   "author": "dd632bd3bbcdd7e9",
   "date": "2020-03-11T19:37:57Z",
   "subject": "Re: Spatial hierarchy",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">Thanks for the good answer.  We sometimes refer to that as &quot;nested indexing&quot;, but &quot;grid lookup&quot; also makes sense.<div><br></div><div>Small technical note:  It is better to provide id_LADs as constants rather than data.  However, a relatively recent internal feature is that we attempt to check if a vector provided as data is actually used as a constant indexing vector and if so to treat it like part of constants.  So, as long as that feature works, it shouldn&#39;t matter anymore, but still one might argue there is a conceptual clarity in providing it as constants.</div><div><br></div><div>-Perry</div></div><br><div class=\"gmail_quote\"></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div class=\"gmail_quote\"><div dir=\"ltr\" class=\"gmail_attr\">On Wed, Mar 11, 2020 at 11:46 AM Heather Gaya &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">heather...@gmail.com</a>&gt; wrote:<br></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div class=\"gmail_quote\"><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0px 0px 0px 0.8ex;border-left:1px solid rgb(204,204,204);padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\">One possible solution, if I understand your question correctly, would be to use a &quot;grid lookup&quot; type approach. <div><br></div><div>Give nimble a data object with id_LADs and have it pull from that.  For instance, the object grid.lookup could be a N_LAD X N_LSOA matrix with each entry representing the id for that LAD/LSOA combo. You could then call:</div><div> </div>alpha1[J_LAD,j] ~ dnorm(alpha_LAD[grid.lookup[j_LAD,j]], tau_alpha1) or similar. <div><br></div><div><br><div><br></div><div><div><br></div><div><br>On Wednesday, March 11, 2020 at 2:29:19 PM UTC-4, Theo Rashid wrote:<blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0px 0px 0px 0.8ex;border-left:1px solid rgb(204,204,204);padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\">HI all,<div><br></div><div>I&#39;m building a model with a spatial hierarchy: all LSOAs fit inside a unique LAD. The model is as follows</div><div><br></div><div><div style=\"color:rgb(212,212,212);background-color:rgb(30,30,30);font-family:Menlo,Monaco,&quot;Courier New&quot;,monospace;font-size:12px;line-height:18px;white-space:pre-wrap\"><div><span style=\"color:rgb(156,220,254)\">code</span> &lt;- <span style=\"color:rgb(156,220,254)\">nimbleCode</span>({</div><div>    <span style=\"color:rgb(106,153,85)\"># PRIORS</span></div><br><div>    <span style=\"color:rgb(106,153,85)\"># COMMON TERMS</span></div><div>    <span style=\"color:rgb(156,220,254)\">alpha0</span> <span style=\"color:rgb(86,156,214)\">~</span> <span style=\"color:rgb(220,220,170)\">dnorm</span>(<span style=\"color:rgb(181,206,168)\">0</span>, <span style=\"color:rgb(181,206,168)\">0.00001</span>)</div><div>    <span style=\"color:rgb(156,220,254)\">beta0</span>  <span style=\"color:rgb(86,156,214)\">~</span> <span style=\"color:rgb(220,220,170)\">dnorm</span>(<span style=\"color:rgb(181,206,168)\">0</span>, <span style=\"color:rgb(181,206,168)\">0.00001</span>)</div><div>    </div><div>    <span style=\"color:rgb(106,153,85)\"># AREA TERMS -- random effects for intercepts and slopes</span></div><div>    </div><div>    <span style=\"color:rgb(106,153,85)\"># LAD terms</span></div><div>    <span style=\"color:rgb(197,134,192)\">for</span>(<span style=\"color:rgb(156,220,254)\">j_LAD</span> <span style=\"color:rgb(197,134,192)\">in</span> <span style=\"color:rgb(181,206,168)\">1</span><span style=\"color:rgb(86,156,214)\">:</span><span style=\"color:rgb(156,220,254)\">N_LAD</span>){</div><div>        <span style=\"color:rgb(156,220,254)\">alpha_LAD</span>[<span style=\"color:rgb(156,220,254)\">j_LAD</span>] <span style=\"color:rgb(86,156,214)\">~</span> <span style=\"color:rgb(220,220,170)\">dnorm</span>(<span style=\"color:rgb(156,220,254)\">alpha0</span>, <span style=\"color:rgb(156,220,254)\">tau_alpha_LAD</span>) <span style=\"color:rgb(106,153,85)\"># centred on common terms</span></div><div>        <span style=\"color:rgb(156,220,254)\">beta_LAD</span>[<span style=\"color:rgb(156,220,254)\">j_LAD</span>] <span style=\"color:rgb(86,156,214)\">~</span> <span style=\"color:rgb(220,220,170)\">dnorm</span>(<span style=\"color:rgb(156,220,254)\">beta0</span>, <span style=\"color:rgb(156,220,254)\">tau_beta_LAD</span>)</div><div>    }</div><div>    <span style=\"color:rgb(156,220,254)\">sigma_alpha_LAD</span> <span style=\"color:rgb(86,156,214)\">~</span> <span style=\"color:rgb(220,220,170)\">dunif</span>(<span style=\"color:rgb(181,206,168)\">0</span>,<span style=\"color:rgb(181,206,168)\">2</span>)</div><div>    <span style=\"color:rgb(156,220,254)\">tau_alpha_LAD</span> &lt;- <span style=\"color:rgb(156,220,254)\">pow</span>(<span style=\"color:rgb(156,220,254)\">sigma_alpha_LAD</span>,-<span style=\"color:rgb(181,206,168)\">2</span>)</div><div>    <span style=\"color:rgb(156,220,254)\">sigma_beta_LAD</span>  <span style=\"color:rgb(86,156,214)\">~</span> <span style=\"color:rgb(220,220,170)\">dunif</span>(<span style=\"color:rgb(181,206,168)\">0</span>,<span style=\"color:rgb(181,206,168)\">2</span>)</div><div>    <span style=\"color:rgb(156,220,254)\">tau_beta_LAD</span>  &lt;- <span style=\"color:rgb(156,220,254)\">pow</span>(<span style=\"color:rgb(156,220,254)\">sigma_beta_LAD</span>,-<span style=\"color:rgb(181,206,168)\">2</span>)</div><br><div>    <span style=\"color:rgb(106,153,85)\"># LSOA terms</span></div><div>    <span style=\"color:rgb(197,134,192)\">for</span>(<span style=\"color:rgb(156,220,254)\">j</span> <span style=\"color:rgb(197,134,192)\">in</span> <span style=\"color:rgb(181,206,168)\">1</span><span style=\"color:rgb(86,156,214)\">:</span><span style=\"color:rgb(156,220,254)\">N_LSOA</span>){</div><div>        <span style=\"color:rgb(156,220,254)\">id_LAD</span> &lt;- <span style=\"color:rgb(220,220,170)\">filter</span>(<span style=\"color:rgb(156,220,254)\">mortality_m</span>, <span style=\"color:rgb(156,220,254)\">LSOA.id</span> == <span style=\"color:rgb(156,220,254)\">j</span>)<span style=\"color:rgb(86,156,214)\">$</span><span style=\"color:rgb(156,220,254)\">LAD.id</span>[<span style=\"color:rgb(181,206,168)\">1</span>] <span style=\"color:rgb(106,153,85)\"># picks out LAD for jth LSOA</span></div><div>        <span style=\"color:rgb(156,220,254)\">alpha1</span>[<span style=\"color:rgb(156,220,254)\">j</span>] <span style=\"color:rgb(86,156,214)\">~</span> <span style=\"color:rgb(220,220,170)\">dnorm</span>(<span style=\"color:rgb(156,220,254)\">alpha_LAD</span>[<span style=\"color:rgb(156,220,254)\">id_LAD</span>], <span style=\"color:rgb(156,220,254)\">tau_alpha1</span>) <span style=\"color:rgb(106,153,85)\"># centred on LAD terms</span></div><div>        <span style=\"color:rgb(156,220,254)\">beta1</span>[<span style=\"color:rgb(156,220,254)\">j</span>]  <span style=\"color:rgb(86,156,214)\">~</span> <span style=\"color:rgb(220,220,170)\">dnorm</span>(<span style=\"color:rgb(156,220,254)\">beta_LAD</span>[<span style=\"color:rgb(156,220,254)\">id_LAD</span>], <span style=\"color:rgb(156,220,254)\">tau_beta1</span>)</div><div>    }</div><div>    <span style=\"color:rgb(156,220,254)\">sigma_alpha1</span> <span style=\"color:rgb(86,156,214)\">~</span> <span style=\"color:rgb(220,220,170)\">dunif</span>(<span style=\"color:rgb(181,206,168)\">0</span>,<span style=\"color:rgb(181,206,168)\">2</span>)</div><div>    <span style=\"color:rgb(156,220,254)\">tau_alpha1</span> &lt;- <span style=\"color:rgb(156,220,254)\">pow</span>(<span style=\"color:rgb(156,220,254)\">sigma_alpha1</span>,-<span style=\"color:rgb(181,206,168)\">2</span>)</div><div>    <span style=\"color:rgb(156,220,254)\">sigma_beta1</span>  <span style=\"color:rgb(86,156,214)\">~</span> <span style=\"color:rgb(220,220,170)\">dunif</span>(<span style=\"color:rgb(181,206,168)\">0</span>,<span style=\"color:rgb(181,206,168)\">2</span>)</div><div>    <span style=\"color:rgb(156,220,254)\">tau_beta1</span>  &lt;- <span style=\"color:rgb(156,220,254)\">pow</span>(<span style=\"color:rgb(156,220,254)\">sigma_beta1</span>,-<span style=\"color:rgb(181,206,168)\">2</span>)</div><br><div>    <span style=\"color:rgb(106,153,85)\"># Put all parameters together into indexed lograte</span></div><div>    <span style=\"color:rgb(197,134,192)\">for</span>(<span style=\"color:rgb(156,220,254)\">a</span> <span style=\"color:rgb(197,134,192)\">in</span> <span style=\"color:rgb(181,206,168)\">1</span><span style=\"color:rgb(86,156,214)\">:</span><span style=\"color:rgb(156,220,254)\">N_age_groups</span>){</div><div>        <span style=\"color:rgb(197,134,192)\">for</span>(<span style=\"color:rgb(156,220,254)\">j</span> <span style=\"color:rgb(197,134,192)\">in</span> <span style=\"color:rgb(181,206,168)\">1</span><span style=\"color:rgb(86,156,214)\">:</span><span style=\"color:rgb(156,220,254)\">N_LSOA</span>){</div><div>            <span style=\"color:rgb(197,134,192)\">for</span>(<span style=\"color:rgb(156,220,254)\">t</span> <span style=\"color:rgb(197,134,192)\">in</span> <span style=\"color:rgb(181,206,168)\">1</span><span style=\"color:rgb(86,156,214)\">:</span><span style=\"color:rgb(156,220,254)\">N_year</span>){</div><div>                <span style=\"color:rgb(156,220,254)\">lograte</span>[<span style=\"color:rgb(156,220,254)\">a</span>, <span style=\"color:rgb(156,220,254)\">j</span>, <span style=\"color:rgb(156,220,254)\">t</span>] &lt;- <span style=\"color:rgb(156,220,254)\">alpha1</span>[<span style=\"color:rgb(156,220,254)\">j</span>] + <span style=\"color:rgb(156,220,254)\">beta1</span>[<span style=\"color:rgb(156,220,254)\">j</span>] * (<span style=\"color:rgb(156,220,254)\">t</span> - <span style=\"color:rgb(181,206,168)\">8</span>)</div><div>            }</div><div>        }</div><div>    }</div><br><div>    <span style=\"color:rgb(106,153,85)\"># LIKELIHOOD</span></div><div>    <span style=\"color:rgb(106,153,85)\"># N total number of cells, i.e. ages*years*areas(*sex)</span></div><div>    <span style=\"color:rgb(197,134,192)\">for</span> (<span style=\"color:rgb(156,220,254)\">i</span> <span style=\"color:rgb(197,134,192)\">in</span> <span style=\"color:rgb(181,206,168)\">1</span><span style=\"color:rgb(86,156,214)\">:</span><span style=\"color:rgb(156,220,254)\">N</span>) {</div><div>        <span style=\"color:rgb(106,153,85)\"># y is number of deaths in that cell, assumed Poisson </span></div><div>        <span style=\"color:rgb(106,153,85)\"># mu is predicted number of deaths in that cell</span></div><div>        <span style=\"color:rgb(156,220,254)\">y</span>[<span style=\"color:rgb(156,220,254)\">i</span>] <span style=\"color:rgb(86,156,214)\">~</span> <span style=\"color:rgb(220,220,170)\">dpois</span>(<span style=\"color:rgb(156,220,254)\">mu</span>[<span style=\"color:rgb(156,220,254)\">i</span>])</div><div>        <span style=\"color:rgb(220,220,170)\">log</span>(<span style=\"color:rgb(156,220,254)\">mu</span>[<span style=\"color:rgb(156,220,254)\">i</span>]) &lt;- <span style=\"color:rgb(220,220,170)\">log</span>(<span style=\"color:rgb(156,220,254)\">n</span>[<span style=\"color:rgb(156,220,254)\">i</span>]) + <span style=\"color:rgb(156,220,254)\">lograte</span>[<span style=\"color:rgb(156,220,254)\">age</span>[<span style=\"color:rgb(156,220,254)\">i</span>], <span style=\"color:rgb(156,220,254)\">LSOA</span>[<span style=\"color:rgb(156,220,254)\">i</span>], <span style=\"color:rgb(156,220,254)\">yr</span>[<span style=\"color:rgb(156,220,254)\">i</span>]]</div><div>    }</div><div>})</div></div></div><div><br></div><div>Currently I&#39;m using dplyr&#39;s filter method to pick out the right LAD corresponding to the LSOA in that loop (nimble did not like [, ] slicing), but I get the following error:</div><div><br></div><div><pre style=\"font-family:Monaco,monospace,monospace;font-size:12px;outline:none;border-width:initial;border-style:none;word-break:break-all;line-height:1.45;white-space:pre-wrap\"><span><font color=\"#000000\">Error in getSymbolicParentNodesRecurse(x, constNames, indexNames, nimbleFunctionNames,  : \r\n  R function &#39;filter&#39; has arguments that cannot be evaluated; either the function must be a nimbleFunction or values for the following inputs must be specified as constants in the model: mortality_m,LSOA.id.</font></span></pre></div><div><br></div><div>Is there a quick workaround for what seems a fairly straightforward problem of calling the LAD that the LSOA lies within?</div><div><br></div><div>Best,</div><div><br></div><div>Theo</div></div></blockquote></div></div></div></div>\r\n\r\n<p></p></blockquote></div>"
    ],
    [
     1,
     "<div class=\"gmail_quote\"><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0px 0px 0px 0.8ex;border-left:1px solid rgb(204,204,204);padding-left:1ex\">\r\n\r\n-- <br>\r\nYou received this message because you are subscribed to the Google Groups &quot;nimble-users&quot; group.<br>\r\nTo unsubscribe from this group and stop receiving emails from it, send an email to <a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">nimble-users...@googlegroups.com</a>.<br>\r\nTo view this discussion on the web visit <a href=\"https://groups.google.com/d/msgid/nimble-users/34da3211-83b4-4cfd-bfd4-ac094e8ecedb%40googlegroups.com?utm_medium=email&amp;utm_source=footer\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://groups.google.com/d/msgid/nimble-users/34da3211-83b4-4cfd-bfd4-ac094e8ecedb%2540googlegroups.com?utm_medium%3Demail%26utm_source%3Dfooter&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792478161767000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0fyAZOORxpUl2K1qCosdi4\">https://groups.google.com/d/msgid/nimble-users/34da3211-83b4-4cfd-bfd4-ac094e8ecedb%40googlegroups.com</a>.<br>\r\n</blockquote></div>\r\n"
